---
description: Next.js React components must be arrow functions with a single responsibility
globs: web/src/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# React components (web)

- Export **functional components as arrow functions**. Do not use `function ComponentName()`.
- Route files (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`) follow the same rule: `const Page = () => {}` then `export default Page`.
- Each component does **one thing**. If it mixes layout, data fetching UI, and a form, split it.
- Put split pieces in the **same folder** as the parent, one component per file.
- Name files after the component: `ChatWindow.tsx` exports `ChatWindow`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — function declaration, mixed concerns
export default function ChatTestPage() {
  return (
    <div>
      <StorePicker />
      <MessageList />
      <Composer />
    </div>
  );
}

// ✅ GOOD — arrow component; page only composes
const ChatTestPage = () => (
  <div>
    <StorePicker />
    <MessageList />
    <Composer />
  </div>
);

export default ChatTestPage;
```

Folder after a split (feature stays together):

```
components/chat/
  ChatWindow.tsx
  MessageList.tsx
  Composer.tsx
```
